---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import benchmarks from '../data/benchmarks.json';
import sources from '../data/sources.json';
const sourceById = new Map(sources.map((source) => [source.id, source]));
const agentRows = benchmarks.filter((row) => row.benchmark === 'Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index').sort((a,b) => b.score-a.score);
const modelRows = benchmarks.filter((row) => row.kind === 'model-intelligence').sort((a,b) => b.score-a.score);
const terminalRows = benchmarks.filter((row) => row.benchmark === 'Terminal-Bench').sort((a,b) => b.score-a.score);
const agents = [...new Set(agentRows.map((row) => row.agent))].sort();
---
<BaseLayout title="External benchmarks" description="Externally published coding-agent and model-intelligence results with cost per task, cost per expected pass, token economics, speed, and Pareto membership.">
  <section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">External results only</p><h1>Quality remains attached to the tested model, harness, and benchmark.</h1><p class="lede">The dashboard imports publisher-owned values and derives transparent ratios from them. It does not run a private suite, infer scores for untested subscription routes, or treat an Intelligence Index as a task pass rate.</p></section>
  <section class="section compact"><div class="callout"><strong>Cost per expected pass is available only for pass-rate-like coding-agent scores.</strong> It equals API cost per task divided by score/100; failed attempts remain in the economics. Model Intelligence Index rows instead use blended dollars per million tokens per intelligence point.</div></section>

  <section class="section compact">
    <div class="toolbar"><div class="control"><label for="benchmark-search">Search benchmark rows</label><input id="benchmark-search" data-benchmark-search type="search" placeholder="Agent or model…" /></div><div class="control"><label for="benchmark-agent">Agent</label><select id="benchmark-agent" data-benchmark-agent><option value="all">All agents</option>{agents.map((agent) => <option value={agent}>{agent}</option>)}</select></div></div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="table-shell"><table data-benchmark-table><thead><tr><th>Agent / model</th><th>Index</th><th>API cost/task</th><th>API $/expected pass</th><th>Passes/API $</th><th>Time/task</th><th>Minutes/expected pass</th><th>Pareto</th></tr></thead><tbody>{agentRows.map((row) => <tr data-benchmark-row data-agent={row.agent} data-search={`${row.agent} ${row.model}`.toLowerCase()}><td><strong>{row.agent}</strong><span class="cell-sub">{row.model}</span></td><td class="numeric">{row.score}</td><td class="numeric">{row.apiCostPerTaskUsd != null ? `$${row.apiCostPerTaskUsd.toFixed(2)}` : '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{row.apiUsdPerExpectedPass != null ? `$${row.apiUsdPerExpectedPass.toFixed(3)}` : '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{row.expectedPassesPerApiDollar?.toFixed(3) ?? '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{row.timePerTaskMinutes != null ? `${row.timePerTaskMinutes.toFixed(1)}m` : '—'}</td><td class="numeric">{row.minutesPerExpectedPass != null ? `${row.minutesPerExpectedPass.toFixed(1)}m` : '—'}</td><td>{row.costQualityPareto && <span class="pareto-chip">cost</span>} {row.timeQualityPareto && <span class="pareto-chip">time</span>} {row.tokenQualityPareto && <span class="pareto-chip">tokens</span>}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Model-level evidence</p><h2>Intelligence, blended price, and speed</h2></div><p>The 7:2:1 blended price weights cache reads, fresh input, and output according to Artificial Analysis’s published convention. The ratio is comparable only within that convention and benchmark version.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="table-shell"><table><thead><tr><th>Provider / model</th><th>Intelligence</th><th>Input/M</th><th>Cache/M</th><th>Output/M</th><th>7:2:1 blended/M</th><th>$/M/intelligence point</th><th>Speed</th><th>Pareto</th></tr></thead><tbody>{modelRows.map((row) => <tr><td><strong>{row.model}</strong><span class="cell-sub">{row.provider}</span></td><td class="numeric">{row.score}</td><td class="numeric">${row.inputPricePerMUsd?.toFixed(3)}</td><td class="numeric">${row.cachedInputPricePerMUsd?.toFixed(3)}</td><td class="numeric">${row.outputPricePerMUsd?.toFixed(3)}</td><td class="numeric">${row.blendedPricePerMUsd?.toFixed(3)}</td><td class="numeric">${row.blendedUsdPerIntelligencePoint?.toFixed(5)}</td><td class="numeric">{row.outputTokensPerSecond != null ? `${row.outputTokensPerSecond.toFixed(1)} t/s` : '—'}</td><td>{row.priceIntelligencePareto && <span class="pareto-chip">price</span>} {row.speedIntelligencePareto && <span class="pareto-chip">speed</span>}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="section-kicker">Separate benchmark</p><h2>Terminal-Bench 2.1</h2></div><p>These pass rates are retained as their own benchmark and are not blended into the Coding Agent Index or model Intelligence Index.</p></div><div class="insight-grid">{terminalRows.map((row) => <article class="insight-card"><div class="metric">{row.score}%</div><h3>{row.agent}</h3><p>{row.model}</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="section compact"><div class="callout warning"><strong>Plan transfer requires evidence.</strong> A model result can inform a plan’s quality signal when the checkpoint matches, but native-agent task-capacity calculations are published only when the tested harness and a quantified subscription denominator can be joined directly.</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
